  "notes": "Captured with WebFetch on 2026-10-13. robots.txt blocked WebFetch for /searchresults, /cart, /login (and auth.game.co.uk) and /accountinformation; their expectations come from research/game-uk.md (2026-09-29 browser capture). The header account dropdown links (Account details, Track orders, Manage payments, Address book, Change password, Contact preferences) are in the real header markup. The mega-menu column contents were not in the fetched HTML, so header items list the department links only; the seasonal \"Christmas & Gifting\" entry (it links to the homepage) is skipped. Help centre links (help.game.co.uk), Careers (frasers.group) and the App Store / Google Play badges are off-site on the real site and become local pages. The real /sitemap page is a category directory; sitemap items use its Categories tree (top level and main children; third-level and Black Friday/Christmas/Events children omitted) plus the header departments and main non-product sections. /pc-gaming, /tech, /lego, /playstation and /nintendo have no H1 on the real site; their page titles/H2 stand in. Reference mode also carries a ~300-row shop-floor assortment (stores/game-uk/shelf-data.js) read from the live listing pages on 2026-10-13 (/playstation/games, /xbox/games, /nintendo/games, /coming-soon, /accessories, /consoles, /digital, PC and tech accessory pages, toys, trading cards, LEGO); the homepage Trending row matches the live one (GTA VI, FC27, Star Wars Galactic Racer, Yu-Gi-Oh! Beyond the Brave). The GTA VI rows remain the only evidence-backed catalog rows.",
